2026-09-07T12:39:05.5852746Z   PR_BODY: Unexpected TLC outcomes previously lost the F# runner's full streams/state/crash files, and the TypeScript runner could retry an in-run JVM failure over reused paths. Both runners now give every attempt an owned source workspace and retain complete unexpected-run diagnostics. Only an ordinary, explicitly pre-TLC JVM initialization exit can retry; every earlier failure remains preserved.

The runtime identity probe has its own crash/stream files and a complete capture deadline. Synthetic fixtures cover inherited pipes, metadata-only fatal/timeout outcomes, working-tree helper admission, ignored-input refusal, exclusive file creation and cleanup isolation. CI uploads the owned diagnostic directory with hidden files and seven-day retention. Unexpected local directories have no automatic purge.

Validation: 45 focused TypeScript tests (202 expectations), strict typecheck and 18 F# synthetic/metadata tests, including the CI-pinned Bun 1.3.13. The parent-executed combined integration at `457bdf094f368eb9e6f2b359b72e5677fd015eb3` passed the mapped Release build with zero warnings/errors and the full solution with 7,552 passes, six existing skips and no failures; all 52 pinned TLC cases passed. Its exact input hashes, full logs and seven TRX archives are copied into this repair's self-contained validation record. That total belongs to the larger C1-policy/retention/hidden-switch integration, not a claim that the same total ran in this smaller writer.

Independent source review accepted `07e399929`; prior TLC and compiler failures remain retained without inferred causes. The repair changes no model, jar, expected state count, model-checker timeout or JVM policy. See [repair report](https://github.com/Lucent-Financial-Group/Zeta/blob/c247403be5d6320b74903e5562b36f55d6884d6f/docs/research/2026-09-07-tlc-attempt-retention.md) and [validation inventory](https://github.com/Lucent-Financial-Group/Zeta/blob/c247403be5d6320b74903e5562b36f55d6884d6f/docs/research/tlc-attempt-retention-validation/2026-09-07/README.md).

C1 PR #16917 is integrated from main. The post-integration comparison verifies 97 of 98 native input hashes exactly; the sole delta is six additional hidden-switch project links in the larger tested integration. The annotated immutable archive `archive/validation/081M1XQM8E4087G0R0036P5RWY-tlc-attempt-retention` resolves to `c247403be5d6320b74903e5562b36f55d6884d6f`, preserving both original source-review pins before branch deletion. All 16 final pre-push checks passed.

